        /// <summary>What would have happened if? Replay the decisions the log recorded over a window (newest first, up to `limit`) with a candidate change applied, and report which would have flipped between allow and deny. Candidates: ABAC policies to add, replace or remove; role permission edits; FGA tuples to write or delete; an access-policy draft (replayed against sampled evaluations). Decisions recorded with `input_mode: full` replay exactly; with `ids`, attributes a policy reads are missing, so each replay first re-decides under the current policies and counts disagreements as `baseline_mismatch`. Nothing is changed. Saved by default; 201 when saved. Needs the decision log on (`PUT /v1/authz_decision_settings`) and an API key that is not limited to organizations.</summary>
